            try {
                doWrite(outboundBuffer);
            } catch (Throwable t) {
                outboundBuffer.failFlushed(t);
                if (t instanceof IOException) {
                    close(voidPromise());
                }
            }
```

So if a write exception occurs (IOException),  it closes the channel.

However, the listeners are called before it closes the channel  (outboundBuffer.failFlushed(t))

I see… And you think the right thing would be to try to read everything left before close ?

